      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Time Off Request Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a time off request form?\", \"a\": \"It is the document an employee uses to ask for specific days or hours away from work. A typical one records the dates, the leave type, the hours charged, and the manager's decision. Some employers call it a leave request form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a time off request form online?\", \"a\": \"Write the policy first, then the fields: dates, hours, leave type, and approver. A time off request form template in Word covers the basics. For a version that also checks balances and shift coverage, Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> builds it from a description of your policy.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide an example of a PTO request form?\", \"a\": \"A simple PTO request form asks for the employee's name, the dates away, the hours charged, and the leave type. Below that sits the manager's approve or decline box. Approved hours then carry over to the time sheet form for that pay period.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I customize a time off request form template?\", \"a\": \"Start from your handbook, not the template. Swap the generic leave types for the ones your policy offers, and note beside each one how much notice it needs and who approves it. Delete any field nobody reads after submit. Emergent can build the customized form from a plain description of that policy and save each request to a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an FMLA leave request form?\", \"a\": \"It is how an employee asks for FMLA leave, the federal entitlement that allows eligible employees up to 12 workweeks of unpaid, job-protected leave in a 12-month period. The form asks when the leave starts and whether it runs as one block or as separate days. Diagnosis details stay off it entirely.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a leave request form and a time off request form?\", \"a\": \"Mostly the name. Leave is the broader word, since it covers absences that are not paid time off, such as jury duty or FMLA leave. One form can handle both when leave type is a required field and each type has its own approver. Pick one name and use it everywhere employees look for the form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I send an employee PTO request form to the right manager?\", \"a\": \"Look the manager up from each person's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/employee-information-form'>employee information form</a> instead of asking the employee to choose. Name a backup approver for the weeks that manager is away, and send medical leave to HR whatever the reporting line says. An app built with Emergent includes every approver, with no per-seat pricing for the backups.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a paid time off request form include sick leave?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as a leave type, though the balance it draws on follows your policy. A pooled policy keeps vacation and sick hours in one bank, and the form shows a single number. A split policy needs two balances, with the leave type choosing which one the request reduces. Allow a start date of today for sick requests; nobody books a fever two weeks out.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I phrase the request to my manager on a time off request form?\", \"a\": \"Name the dates and hours, the leave type, and who covers your work, in two plain sentences. For example: \\\"I'd like to request vacation on June 8-10, 24 hours of PTO. Marcus has agreed to take my client calls while I'm out.\\\" Skip the reason unless your policy asks for one, and send the request as early as the notice period allows.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the notice period for an FMLA leave request form?\", \"a\": \"Employees owe 30 days of notice when the need is foreseeable, such as a planned surgery or the expected birth of a child. The form should still accept a request that starts today, because a lot of leave cannot be planned. Show the 30-day rule beside the start date field before anyone picks a date.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     }
